<article class="boundaries-page page container">
  <header class="boundaries-header text-center">
    <span class="hero-eyebrow">First-Timer Guidance</span>
    <h1>Comfort, Boundaries & Consent</h1>
    <p class="hero-lead" style="max-width: var(--max-paragraph); margin: 0 auto 32px; color: var(--color-espresso-soft);">
      The most important thing to know before arriving at Desire: you decide how far you want to take your vacation. You never have to participate in anything.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Core Reassurance Card -->
  <div class="boundaries-hero-card">
    <h2>The Golden Principle: Participation is Zero-Pressure</h2>
    <p>
      At both Desire Riviera Maya and Desire Pearl, every couple's comfort perimeter is sovereign. 
      Whether you spend your entire week sunbathing in a suit, enjoying quiet dinners, or dancing in the lounge, 
      nobody will question, cajole, or push you.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="boundaries-grid grid-auto-sm max-content mx-auto">
    <section class="boundary-pillar">
      <div class="pillar-icon">01</div>
      <h3>Clothing-Optional Means Truly Optional</h3>
      <p>
        In designated clothing-optional zones (pools, whirlpools, and beaches), you can be fully clothed in resort swimwear, 
        topless, or completely nude. If you want to put your cover-up back on at any point, it is entirely normal.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-pillar">
      <div class="pillar-icon">02</div>
      <h3>Watching & Observing is Completely Normal</h3>
      <p>
        Nearly every couple spends their first 24 to 48 hours getting their bearings. Sitting back with a cocktail, taking in the freedom, 
        and observing the atmosphere is the standard first-timer path. You do not owe anyone an interaction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-pillar">
      <div class="pillar-icon">03</div>
      <h3>A Simple "No" is Absolute and Instant</h3>
      <p>
        Desire guests are exceptionally respectful of boundaries. A warm, polite <em>"Thank you, but we're just enjoying private time together"</em> 
        is universally understood and immediately respected. There is zero awkwardness.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-pillar">
      <div class="pillar-icon">04</div>
      <h3>Clear Policy: Strict Privacy & Photography</h3>
      <p>
        To safeguard guest privacy, cameras, phones, and recording devices are strictly forbidden in all public social, pool, and whirlpool areas. 
        Phones should remain tucked away in beach bags or kept inside your private suite.
      </p>
      <div class="policy-note">
        <strong>Our Concierge Advice:</strong> Treat photography as strictly private. Always follow the resort's official house rules regarding device use.
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- The Couple Alignment Section -->
  <section class="couple-alignment-box">
    <h2>Traveling as a Couple: The 3 Rules Before You Land</h2>
    <ol class="alignment-steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Establish a Safe Word or Signal:</strong> Agree in advance on an effortless way either partner can signal that they need to leave a space, return to the room, or take a breather&mdash;no explanation needed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The Slower Partner Sets the Speed:</strong> The comfort of the partner who wants to move more slowly always governs the trip. Boundaries can tighten or relax naturally over the week.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Debrief at Breakfast:</strong> Every morning over coffee, check in with each other away from music and cocktails to talk about what you enjoyed and what your perimeter is for the day ahead.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

